  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 148 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nIsaias continues to push further east in its track and is expected \nto make landfall this evening. High clouds from Isaias are gradually \nstarting to move into the CWA from the southeast. Lows tonight will \nbe slightly warmer due to the cloud cover, generally in the upper \n50s to near 60. \n\nAs Isaias moves inland the center of the low is expected to move \ninto east KY around Sunday morning. Main impacts for us will be \ntomorrow mainly over western KY, southeast IL, and southwest IN. \nRain chances begin to increase from the southeast around mid morning \ntomorrow. Rain chances peak around 70-100% over western KY Saturday \nafternoon with some bands of 70-80% moving into southern IL by \nSaturday evening. The best chance for any thunderstorms will be \nSaturday afternoon and evening and any severe threat remains well \noff to our southeast. Rain may be heavy at times tomorrow with storm \ntotals up to around 1\" with a few pockets of locally higher amounts \npossible. Sustained winds of 15-25 mph are expected with gusts up to \n30-35 mph. Rain chances then taper off to the east Sunday morning.\n\nAfter a cooler day in the 70s tomorrow, temperatures rebound by \nMonday back into the mid to upper 80s, pushing 90 in some places. \nTemperatures come down slightly for Wednesday and Thursday with a \nstationary front turned warm front draped over the northern portions \nof the area on Wednesday. Rain chances return to the forecast on \nWednesday and increase from the west to 20-40% and continue on \nThursday as a cold front approaches from the west.",
